{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>The tender among you and the delicate.</b> The tender one — he is the delicate one — a term of pampering; and from 'be delicate' (מֵהִתְעַנֵּג) and from 'be tender' (וּמֵרֹךְ) Scripture proves about them that the two are one: even though he is pampered and his sensibility recoils at anything repulsive, the flesh of his sons and daughters will grow sweet to him in his hunger — until <b>his eye be evil</b> toward his surviving sons <b>so that he gives to one of them from the flesh of his sons</b> their brothers <b>that he shall eat.</b> Another interpretation — <b>the tender among you</b>: the compassionate and tender-hearted, out of sheer hunger, will turn cruel and not give from the flesh of their slaughtered sons to their surviving sons."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:42.944399345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}